# Test: the interactive completer offers a plugin's declared pipe alias beside
# the built-in pipe operators.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-10 of spec-plugin-registers-pipe-operations, and User Story 2
#            "types `show ... | ` and reads the names on offer". An operator
#            discovers a pipe name by pressing Tab, so a name nothing offers is
#            a name most operators never meet.
# PREVENTS:  the alias resolving when it is typed in full and never being
#            offered, which is the shape a completer reading only the built-in
#            operator table produces.
#
# Method: a native plugin declares one command and one alias over it in its
# Stage 1 message. A plain ssh client with a pseudo-terminal logs into the
# session model the DAEMON hosts, types the command and a pipe character, and
# presses Tab. Both halves of the offer are asserted: the declared name, and a
# built-in operator beside it. An offer that replaced the operators would pass
# the first assertion and break the surface.
#
# The surface is load-bearing. `ze cli` runs its Bubble Tea model in the CLIENT
# process, where a declared alias does not exist, so the completer there cannot
# answer this and no client-driven test can prove it. The model this drives is
# built by buildSessionModelFactory (cmd/ze/hub/session_factory.go) inside the
# daemon, and its completer reads the registry Stage 1 wrote.
#
# The timeout is DECLARED because this file starts a daemon, waits for an
# external plugin to reach Stage 5, and drives an interactive terminal session.
option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/pipe-alias-completion
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
